sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"57f4ee4af4098391b57a2653b4fdff7ccd0cfc4e34276d375f1dab7427db0027","event_uuid":"8ee13b97-a8bb-4884-98db-c7006aa67862","position":{"commit_sha":"6a2e6f08fb536d6308f9d90c461a0f6a6508d4ad","position":"1787046790208046001-8ee13b97-a8bb-4884-98db-c7006aa67862"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA — CONFIRMED DEFECT\n\nProven root cause: commit d9e0f0e733 replaced standalone-safe raw git subprocesses with unconditional `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter` imports at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py:83` and `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:194`. Both modules are deliberately executable by file path without package context (`_advisory_lock.py:36-52`; `_loader.py:1-34`). In that supported mode the installed wheel intentionally exposes the engine only as `rebar/_engine` package data, so no top-level `rebar_reconciler` package is importable. The first import aborts `_lock_remote`; bypassing only it exposes the identical latent failure in `_ref_lock._git`.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof:\n- Exact held-out test fails deterministically at `_advisory_lock.py:83`; post-mortem state was `__name__ == \"_bridge_preview_advisory_lock\"`, `__package__ == \"\"`, no `rebar_reconciler` in `sys.modules`, and `find_spec(\"rebar_reconciler\") is None`.\n- In a real temporary git repo, loading the module exactly by path and replacing only `_lock_remote` with a local lambda advanced to `_ref_lock.py:194` and raised the same `ModuleNotFoundError`, proving both seams participate.\n- Seeding the supported embedded package through `_lib_ops._engine_module(\"rebar_reconciler.git_adapter\")` made the exact interface test pass (1 passed), ruling out git_adapter behavior and lock/contention logic.\n- A fresh installed wheel reports ordinary `find_spec(\"rebar_reconciler\") is None` by design, while both `_lib_ops._engine_module(...)` and an `engine_env()` subprocess load it successfully; packaging is not omitted accidentally (`pyproject.toml:68-70,304-310`; `src/rebar/_engine.py:78-100`).\n- The pre-d9 parent commit, with the same ordinary import result of None, successfully acquired and released a real standalone ref lock. This pins the regression to d9e0f0e733 rather than the later held-out test loader.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. The module and shared loader explicitly promise standalone by-path execution, and the pre-d9 runtime proves that behavior existed before the centralization refactor. The existing held-out interface test is the authoritative preview-under-contention contract. H2 (unsupported test loader) is rejected by those explicit contracts and multiple by-path callers; H3 (packaging omission) is rejected by the documented package-data/engine_env design and fresh-wheel probe.\n\nExpected repair target: route both git_adapter loads through the already-supported by-path lazy loader without expanding packaging or weakening the interface oracle.","timestamp":1787046236432971001}],"created_at":1787045478766940001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"734004ac-fe50-42e6-99fb-1536d6669825","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9918-a5d6-8fb5-42e8"}],"description":"## Context\nWhile broadening verification for runty-effectible-bluewhale on current origin/main, `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py::test_preview_is_complete_while_sync_locks_are_held` failed deterministically, both in the 443-test store suite and alone. `_advisory_lock._lock_remote` imports `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter`, but that top-level package is intentionally unavailable in the normal installed in-process environment, raising `ModuleNotFoundError` before the lock behavior executes. This is unrelated to attach-commits code-root changes.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nCommit `d9e0f0e733` introduced unconditional top-level `git_adapter` imports at `_advisory_lock.py:83` and `_ref_lock.py:194`, breaking the explicit standalone by-path loading contract in `_advisory_lock.py` and `_loader.py`. Runtime experiments confirmed both failure sites; the pre-refactor parent succeeds with the same absent top-level package; supported package-seeded paths remain green. The full proof is recorded in the Phase 1 RCA comment.\n\n## Repair Plan\n- At both confirmed seams, load the sibling with exactly `git_adapter = lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler.git_adapter\", \"git_adapter.py\")`. The dotted key is mandatory: it is the same `sys.modules` key registered by unchanged package-context imports in `_concurrency.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, `apply_outbound.py`, and `__main__.py`, so the repaired and unchanged paths share one module object.\n- Preserve package-loaded behavior, adapter API identity, lock semantics, and intentional wheel packaging.\n- Do not use a mangled cache key, change the interface oracle, or add test-only `sys.path`/package seeding.\n\n## Testing\n- Use the existing failing held-out interface test as the RED oracle because it crosses both real standalone load seams and exercises a real ref-lock acquire/check/release around bridge preview.\n- Hold the oracle out from the fixer, then require GREEN; mutate each repaired seam back to the exact absolute import and require RED; restore and require GREEN.\n- Add a package-context identity assertion that package import and both repaired lazy-load seams resolve the same `sys.modules[\"rebar_reconciler.git_adapter\"]` module object, including a module-qualified monkeypatch observed by the repaired seam.\n- Run the exact original reproduction, advisory/ref-lock tests, the broader store interface suite, and project lint/typecheck gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The exact held-out contention test passes in isolation without test-only path pollution.\n- [ ] Both standalone seams use exactly `lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler.git_adapter\", \"git_adapter.py\")`.\n- [ ] A package-context test proves the repaired seams and unchanged importers share one git_adapter module object and observe the same module-qualified monkeypatch.\n- [ ] Defect-seeded mutation of either seam returns the held-out oracle to RED.\n- [ ] The broader store suite passes.\n- [ ] Lint and typecheck pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py","reason":"Restore standalone-safe git_adapter loading in lock-remote resolution using the canonical dotted cache key."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py","reason":"Restore standalone-safe git_adapter loading in the nested ref-lock git seam using the same canonical dotted cache key."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py","reason":"Prove package-context module identity and module-qualified monkeypatch visibility across the repaired loader seam."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1cf6db6b-b228-4437-96d7-0fb3527080b6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["test","bridge","reconciler"],"ticket_id":"79c6-eaf3-38af-4ce9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bridge preview lock test cannot import reconciler package","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["69061069-2ac8-4042-983a-64a7ed732a70","734004ac-fe50-42e6-99fb-1536d6669825","559b2553-4318-4ccc-a72d-1e95fa863991","1cf6db6b-b228-4437-96d7-0fb3527080b6","75768ca9-39e6-4285-9e13-223540e6332c","26c381fd-345b-4369-afbd-d607b49090a5","c98c4083-59c6-46ec-a15f-a547f1fb63f5","99a3f7fc-804c-4225-a618-70e8f18385b1","8daaa488-8d06-4663-bb04-e76ac0e31805","e7d9f8d6-80b6-4683-b348-9b2729ec4ca1","8ee13b97-a8bb-4884-98db-c7006aa67862"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787048630355990001,"uuid":"99e61baa-f974-493a-a1a7-0bf7627e59bc"}